### Create person → expect 201
POST http://localhost:7500/api/persons
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@test.com",
  "password": "secret",
  "name": "John",
  "age": 30
}

### Get person by ID → expect 200
GET http://localhost:7500/api/persons/1

### Get all non-admin persons → expect 200 with array
GET http://localhost:7500/api/persons

### Update person name and age → expect 200
PUT http://localhost:7500/api/persons/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Updated",
  "age": 31
}

### Duplicate email → expect 409 with EMAIL_ALREADY_EXISTS
POST http://localhost:7500/api/persons
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@test.com",
  "password": "secret",
  "name": "John",
  "age": 30
}

### Person not found → expect 404 with PERSON_NOT_FOUND
GET http://localhost:7500/api/persons/999

### Update non-existing person → expect 404 with PERSON_NOT_FOUND
PUT http://localhost:7500/api/persons/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ghost",
  "age": 40
}
